---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

// Display photos for Sage Foundation
const displayPhotos = [
  "/sage1.jpg",
  "/sage2.jpg", 
  "/sage3.jpg",
  "/sage4.jpg"
];
---

<Layout>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
    {/* Back Arrow */}
    <div class="mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center text-primary hover:text-white transition-colors">
        <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Home
      </a>
    </div>

    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="mb-6 font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-white">
        Sage Literacy Foundation
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12 text-center">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Foundation Overview</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral">Sage Literacy Foundation is an initiative I founded at age 13, to promote literacy and education in underserved communities. Through book donations and educational workshops, we aim to provide resources and opportunities for students to develop their reading and language skills.</p>
      </section>

      {/* Display Photos Gallery */}
      <div class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-6 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Media</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          {displayPhotos.map((photo, index) => (
            <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-neutral/20 cursor-pointer transition-all duration-300 hover:scale-105 hover:border-primary/30" onclick={`openImageModal('${photo}', 'Sage Literacy Foundation initiative ${index + 1}')`}>
              <Image
                src={photo}
                alt={`Sage Literacy Foundation initiative ${index + 1}`}
                width={200}
                height={200}
                class="h-40 w-full object-cover"
              />
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-12 text-center">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Initiatives & Impact</h2>
        <ul class="text-neutral list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Book donations to Nagie's Angels Educational Centre in Kumasi</li>
          <li>One-week English Language workshop at Labadi Presby/Emmause JHS</li>
          <li>Community engagement and volunteer coordination</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* LinkedIn Post Embed */}
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-6 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary text-center">Recent Impact</h2>
        <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          <div class="bg-neutral/10 rounded-lg p-6 border border-neutral/20">
            <div class="flex items-center mb-4">
              <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-primary/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3">
                <span class="text-primary font-bold text-sm">SA</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-white font-medium">Shifa Amankwa-Gabbey</h3>
                <p class="text-neutral text-sm">CE @ Ashesi • 1y</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="text-neutral text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
              <p class="mb-3">Erica Ayeyi Amoa Atta and I first met at Ashesi's writing centre, where I needed to proofread my first reflection paper due in two days. As we were scanning through, one of the paragraphs mentioned my nonprofit, Sage Literacy Foundation. This opened a conversation and Ayeyi was eager to hear more about the work we do.</p>
              
              <p class="mb-3">After the one-hour proofreading session we had, we found ourselves discussing Sage and her year three Leadership Service-Learning Project. It eventually advanced to how she would love to clock in forty hours of her time working with my nonprofit. I was deeply honoured and delighted when she made that proposal, regardless of the fact that I had never done anything of the sort.</p>
              
              <p class="mb-3">We spent the next three weeks organising the undertaking of the project; location, duration and logistics. After weeks of thorough planning, we settled on a one-week reading and writing workshop for JHS 2 and 3 students of Labadi Presby/Emmause Junior High School.</p>
              
              <p class="mb-3">It was the warm reception by the students on our first day that gave me a conviction that I was going to love every moment of this. They were very excited to engage in what we were going to take them through. We printed web articles to engage them in read-aloud sessions, comprehension passages and flyers with grammar tips.</p>
              
              <p class="mb-3">We did a BECE simulation and held timed free writing exercises in all four taught classes. I taught the students important discrepancies between the two major varieties of English, basic grammar and spelling rules as well as tips for general preparation for the BECE English Language paper.</p>
              
              <p class="mb-3">We wrapped everything up by pasting educational flyers on the classrooms' walls and finally doing a mini donation of books to the school's library. The more we advanced in the project, the more I realised how much of a pleasure it was working with Ayeyi. She is a brilliant, innovative individual whose dedication and passion towards community service are commendable!</p>
              
              <p>I am grateful for the growth of Sage, and that I get to share my love for reading and writing in so many ways! <span class="text-primary">#Literacy #LittleSteps2024</span></p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-neutral/70">
              <div class="flex items-center space-x-4">
                <span>👍 72</span>
                <span>💬 10 Comments</span>
              </div>
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7172283375720820736/" target="_blank" class="text-primary hover:text-white transition-colors">
                View on LinkedIn →
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="flex justify-center">
        <a href="https://instagram.com/sageliteracyfoundation" target="_blank" class="rounded-full bg-primary px-8 py-4 text-white font-medium hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors after:ml-2 after:content-[url(/external.svg)]">
          Follow on Instagram
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- Image Modal -->
  <div id="imageModal" class="fixed inset-0 z-50 hidden bg-black/90 backdrop-blur-sm">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-center min-h-screen p-4">
      <div class="relative max-w-4xl max-h-[90vh]">
        <button 
          id="closeModal" 
          class="absolute -top-12 right-0 text-white hover:text-primary transition-colors text-2xl font-bold z-10"
          onclick="closeImageModal()"
        >
          ✕
        </button>
        <img id="modalImage" src="" alt="" class="max-w-full max-h-full object-contain rounded-lg" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    function openImageModal(src: string, alt: string) {
      const modal = document.getElementById('imageModal');
      const modalImage = document.getElementById('modalImage') as HTMLImageElement;
      
      if (!modal || !modalImage) return;
      
      modalImage.src = src;
      modalImage.alt = alt;
      modal.classList.remove('hidden');
      document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
    }

    function closeImageModal() {
      const modal = document.getElementById('imageModal');
      if (!modal) return;
      
      modal.classList.add('hidden');
      document.body.style.overflow = 'auto';
    }

    // Close modal when clicking outside the image
    const modalElement = document.getElementById('imageModal');
    if (modalElement) {
      modalElement.addEventListener('click', (e: Event) => {
        const target = e.target as HTMLElement;
        if (target && target.id === 'imageModal') {
          closeImageModal();
        }
      });
    }

    // Close modal with Escape key
    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
      if (e.key === 'Escape') {
        closeImageModal();
      }
    });
  </script>
</Layout>